## 2. Normalizing flows for the causal graph

> Second, I need to finally explicitly add the Normalizing flows for the causal graph to the model. Note that you should pay attention to normalization over dataset, needs for normalizing flow training, being general so it is dataset agnostic and ...

Goal: replace the current editing scheme (flip one attribute's conditioning index,
independently of the rest) with real structural-causal-model counterfactuals: abduct
exogenous noise per attribute, intervene on the target, propagate the predicted effect to
causal descendants via normalizing flows, then condition HDAE on the full resulting
attribute vector.

Plan:
- Declare a causal DAG over the conditioning attributes (see open decision below).
- One flow per attribute node, conditioned on its parents (masked-autoregressive-flow-per-
  node / "Deep SCM" pattern), fit on the packed attribute table
  (`data/packed/*_attrs.npz`) — not on images. New module, e.g.
  `experiments/hdae/causal/scm.py` (fit/sample/abduct/intervene) +
  `experiments/hdae/causal/normalize.py` (per-attribute normalization).
- Dataset-agnostic by construction: the flow only needs a labeled attribute table + a
  declared DAG, so the same code should work on CelebA-HQ, MorphoMNIST, and
  Causal3DIdent (item 3) without dataset-specific branches beyond the normalization layer.
- Integration point: in `run_pcf_eval.py::evaluate_intervention` (or its item-1-refactored
  equivalent), replace the single-attribute `y_cf[:, target_col] = 1/0` flip with:
  abduct noise from the source image's real attributes -> set the target attribute ->
  forward through the flow to get counterfactual values for its descendants -> condition
  HDAE on the whole resulting vector, not just the one flipped entry.
- New training script `experiments/hdae/causal/train_scm.py`, run once per dataset,
  independent of and prior to HDAE training/inference.

Depends on: item 1 (cleaner if `intervene()` in the adapter contract can take a full
attribute vector, not just one flipped index) — do item 1 first, matches your ordering.

Open decisions (your call, not guessing these):
- The DAG itself (e.g. is `Young` a parent of `Male`? is `Eyeglasses` downstream of
  `Smiling`?) — a modeling/domain claim, needs your judgment.
- Flow library — nothing is installed yet (checked venv + requirements, no `nflows`/
  `zuko`/`FrEIA`/`pyro`). Leaning `nflows` (lightweight, MAF/RealNVP, PyTorch-native)
  unless you have a preference.
- CelebA's attributes are binary; a continuous-flow framework needs either a
  logit-transform of smoothed empirical probability or a discrete/categorical flow
  variant. Affects item 3's continuous factors differently too — worth deciding once.


